Local Optimize on Debian/Ubuntu
================================

The package installs application code in /usr/lib/local-optimize, the
/usr/bin/local-optimize CLI and inactive systemd user units. It does not
create databases, secrets, model directories, virtual environments or agent
configuration, and it does not enable or start services.

Create a per-user Python environment after installing the package:

  python3 -m venv ~/.local/share/local-optimize/venv
  ~/.local/share/local-optimize/venv/bin/python -m pip install --upgrade pip
  ~/.local/share/local-optimize/venv/bin/python -m pip install --no-deps \
    -r /usr/lib/local-optimize/deploy/intel-xpu-requirements.txt
  ~/.local/share/local-optimize/venv/bin/python -m pip install \
    -r /usr/lib/local-optimize/requirements.txt

Install the model snapshots and Ollama model, create the PostgreSQL database
and ~/.config/local-optimize/secrets.env as described in
/usr/share/doc/local-optimize/docs/installation.md. Replace repository paths
in that guide with /usr/lib/local-optimize where appropriate.

Commands:

  local-optimize migrate        Apply database migrations
  local-optimize server         Run the FastAPI server
  local-optimize watchdog       Run filesystem indexing
  local-optimize mcp            Run the full local-only MCP server
  local-optimize lmstudio-mcp   Run the read-only LM Studio wrapper
  local-optimize index          Index the registered project

LOCAL_OPTIMIZE_VENV can override ~/.local/share/local-optimize/venv.
LOCAL_OPTIMIZE_ROOT can override /usr/lib/local-optimize for packaging checks.

The user units are templates only:

  systemctl --user enable --now gpu-rag-server.service watchdog-indexer.service

Enable them only after completing runtime setup and health checks. Agent
installation and migration to a new engine are intentionally separate tasks.
